2. Component Breakdown

2.1 Data Layer — Tick DB Integration

The tick DB is external to the simulator but is the source of truth for all replay.

Component Responsibility Interface
Tick DB Client Reads market data (MBO/MBP), order events, fill events from the existing tick DB TickDbReader — returns ordered stream of MarketEvent and OrderEvent
Event Cursor Maintains replay position; supports seeking to timestamp EventCursor.seek(timestamp), EventCursor.next()
Data Normalizer Converts tick DB schema to internal SimEvent format EventNormalizer — schema-agnostic, pluggable per venue

Key design decision: The simulator does not own the tick DB. It consumes it via a read-only interface. This keeps replay deterministic (same DB state → same results) and allows the tick DB to evolve independently.

Java 11 note: Use java.nio.ByteBuffer / FileChannel for memory-mapped reads if the tick DB exposes raw files; otherwise, a thin JDBC/java.sql layer over a columnar store. Avoid ORM frameworks — they introduce non-determinism and latency jitter.

