2.4 Algo Under Test (Pluggable)

Purpose: The strategy being tested. The simulator is agnostic to its logic — it only requires a defined interface.

Interface method Called when
onMarketData(MarketDataEvent) Every market data update
onFill(FillEvent) A fill occurs on any of the algo's orders
onTimer(TimerEvent) Scheduled timer fires (e.g., cancel-after-N-ms)
onOrderUpdate(OrderActionEvent) Ack/reject/modify confirmation from venue
getPendingActions() Simulator polls for new actions (post, cancel, modify)

Design rule: The algo is a pure function of its inputs. It must not call System.currentTimeMillis(), open network connections, or read external state. Time comes from the event stream .

Java 11 note: Define the algo interface as an abstract class, not an interface, to allow default state (position, open orders). Use enum for action types to avoid String comparisons.

---

2.5 Event Log (Append-Only Journal)

Purpose: Every event — market data consumed, decision made, action taken, fill received — is logged. This is the ground truth for replay, reconciliation, and evidence generation.

Aspect Design
Format Binary or Parquet; append-only; immutable
Schema timestamp_ns, event_type, symbol, order_id, price, quantity, side, state_before, state_after, metadata
Writer Async writer on a separate thread (off hot path)
Retention Configurable; minimum 1 trading year for compliance
Reprocessing The event log alone is sufficient to reconstruct any run

Java 11 impl: Use java.nio.channels.FileChannel with a dedicated writer thread. Buffer events in a RingBuffer and flush periodically. Avoid FileWriter (synchronized) .

